{
  "name": "laplace-lang",
  "displayName": "Laplace Language Support",
  "description": "Syntax highlighting, semantic coloring, autocomplete, live diagnostics, and rendered @math doc formulas for .laplace and .laplacelib files (a source-to-source preprocessor for Stan). Works unmodified in Positron via Open VSX.",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "license": "MIT",
  "publisher": "laplace-lang",
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.85.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Programming Languages"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "laplace",
    "laplacelib",
    "stan",
    "bayesian",
    "statistics",
    "language server"
  ],
  "activationEvents": [
    "onLanguage:laplace",
    "onLanguage:laplacelib"
  ],
  "main": "./out/extension.js",
  "contributes": {
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "laplace.toggleUnsupportedSyntaxDiagnostics",
        "title": "Toggle diagnostics from unsupported (patch-1) syntax",
        "category": "Laplace"
      },
      {
        "command": "laplace.toggleRenderMath",
        "title": "Toggle rendering of //@math doc formulas",
        "category": "Laplace"
      }
    ],
    "languages": [
      {
        "id": "laplace",
        "aliases": [
          "Laplace",
          "laplace"
        ],
        "extensions": [
          ".laplace"
        ],
        "configuration": "./language-configuration.json"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplacelib",
        "aliases": [
          "Laplace Library",
          "laplacelib"
        ],
        "extensions": [
          ".laplacelib"
        ],
        "configuration": "./language-configuration.json"
      }
    ],
    "grammars": [
      {
        "language": "laplace",
        "scopeName": "source.laplace",
        "path": "./syntaxes/laplace.tmLanguage.json"
      },
      {
        "language": "laplacelib",
        "scopeName": "source.laplacelib",
        "path": "./syntaxes/laplacelib.tmLanguage.json"
      }
    ],
    "snippets": [
      {
        "language": "laplace",
        "path": "./snippets/laplace.json"
      },
      {
        "language": "laplacelib",
        "path": "./snippets/laplacelib.json"
      }
    ],
    "semanticTokenTypes": [
      {
        "id": "laplaceData",
        "description": "Identifier declared in a `data` block"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceParameter",
        "description": "Identifier declared in a `parameters` block"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceTransformedParameter",
        "description": "Identifier declared in a `transformed parameters` block"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceGeneratedQuantity",
        "description": "Identifier declared in a `generated quantities` block"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceLocal",
        "description": "Identifier declared in `transformed data` or as a local"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceBuiltinFunction",
        "description": "Call to a Stan built-in function"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceLibraryFunction",
        "description": "Call to an imported library function (`pkg::func`)"
      },
      {
        "id": "laplaceUserFunction",
        "description": "Call to a function defined in this file's `functions {}` block"
      }
    ],
    "semanticTokenScopes": [
      {
        "language": "laplace",
        "scopes": {
          "laplaceData": [
            "variable.other.readwrite.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceParameter": [
            "variable.parameter.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceTransformedParameter": [
            "variable.other.property.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceGeneratedQuantity": [
            "variable.other.member.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceLocal": [
            "variable.other.local.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceBuiltinFunction": [
            "support.function.builtin.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceLibraryFunction": [
            "support.function.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceUserFunction": [
            "entity.name.function.laplace"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "language": "laplacelib",
        "scopes": {
          "laplaceData": [
            "variable.other.readwrite.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceParameter": [
            "variable.parameter.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceTransformedParameter": [
            "variable.other.property.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceGeneratedQuantity": [
            "variable.other.member.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceLocal": [
            "variable.other.local.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceBuiltinFunction": [
            "support.function.builtin.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceLibraryFunction": [
            "support.function.laplace"
          ],
          "laplaceUserFunction": [
            "entity.name.function.laplace"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "iconThemes": [
      {
        "id": "laplace-seti",
        "label": "Laplace",
        "path": "./icons/seti/vs-seti-icon-theme.json"
      }
    ],
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Laplace",
      "properties": {
        "laplace.serverPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "laplace-lsp",
          "description": "Path to the laplace-lsp executable. Defaults to `laplace-lsp` on PATH."
        },
        "laplace.trace.server": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "off",
            "messages",
            "verbose"
          ],
          "default": "off",
          "description": "Trace communication between VS Code and laplace-lsp (for debugging the extension itself)."
        },
        "laplace.docs.renderMath": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Render the `//@math` section of a doc comment as a formula in hover tooltips, instead of showing the raw LaTeX. Rendering runs locally (MathJax, bundled -- no network). Turn it off to see the LaTeX source as written."
        },
        "laplace.diagnostics.unsupportedSyntax": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Show diagnostics that Laplace patch-1 syntax provokes from a compiler that does not accept it yet. Set to `false` while rewriting a library in the new syntax.\n\nOnly diagnostics **caused by** patch-1 syntax are hidden, and each rule is anchored to the syntax that causes it:\n\n- \"cannot contain a `model` block\", but only on a `@macro` header line. A real `model` block in a `.laplacelib` is still reported.\n- \"`pkg::name` is not in `pkg`'s exports\", but only on a line carrying `@use` or `@expand`. A mistyped `pkg::func` anywhere else is still reported.\n- `stanc` diagnostics, but only from the first line containing patch-1 syntax onward. `stanc` stops at its first error, so a missing `;` **above** a template keeps its squiggle, and a file with no patch-1 syntax at all is untouched.\n\nUnresolved imports, version conflicts and uninstalled packages are always reported. Changing this restarts the language server so already-published diagnostics are recomputed.\n\nOne limit no editor-side filter can lift: when patch-1 syntax comes first in a file, `stanc` stops there and never parses the rest, so ordinary Stan mistakes further down go unreported until the compiler learns the syntax."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "scripts": {
    "vscode:prepublish": "npm run compile -- --production",
    "compile": "node esbuild.js",
    "watch": "node esbuild.js --watch",
    "check": "tsc --noEmit -p ./",
    "test:unit": "node esbuild.js --tests && node --test out/test",
    "test:grammar": "vscode-tmgrammar-snap \"fixtures/**/*.laplace\" \"fixtures/**/*.laplacelib\"",
    "test:grammar:update": "vscode-tmgrammar-snap -u \"fixtures/**/*.laplace\" \"fixtures/**/*.laplacelib\"",
    "test": "npm run check && npm run test:unit && npm run test:grammar && npm run test:bundle",
    "package": "npm run compile -- --production && npx --yes @vscode/vsce package --no-dependencies",
    "test:bundle": "npm run compile && node scripts/check-bundle.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "mathjax-full": "^3.2.1",
    "vscode-languageclient": "^9.0.1"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/node": "^20.11.0",
    "@types/vscode": "^1.85.0",
    "esbuild": "^0.28.2",
    "typescript": "^5.4.0",
    "vscode-tmgrammar-test": "^0.1.3"
  }
}
